Construction has its many own nuances, with some terrible implications if you get this wrong.

It’s an incredibly tight margin industry, with cash flow having the ability to completely upturn a company.

What's involved?…
🔹 Retentions
🔹 Applications for payment
🔹 Pay less notices
🔹 Variation
…and that’s before too even get to any of the ‘accounting’ part.

There are taxes not seen in any other industry;
🔹CIS scheme domestic reverse charge VAT
🔹 Zero rated
🔹 Reduced rate VAT

And then there’s the personalities, it takes a particular type to not take some of the interactions with subbies and lads on site on their stride.

As specialist in construction Finance with Flow help to make your life smoother by taking the friction out of the day to day processes, taking the worry out of getting the technical stuff wrong and actually help you to improve the margins and cash flow on your projects!

